460 0 obj
<<
/A 1349 0 R
/Alt (Infographic compares hot and cold tumors, illustrating hypoxia-induced PD-L1 upregulation in hot tumors leading to immune attack, and barriers in cold tumors including stromal limits, immune trapping, and chemokine secretion. Potential interventions for cold tumors are shown as cancer vaccines, radio-immunotherapy, photo-immunotherapy, and chemo-immunotherapy. Key tumor microenvironment cell types and components are depicted in a legend, and the central pathway highlighted is immunogenic cell death transforming cold tumors to hot.)
/K [16 1350 0 R]
/P 325 0 R
/Pg 26 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 1)
/Type /StructElem
>>
